Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:15:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - legacy PlayerTeleportEvent and
 PlayerPortalEvent on the async teleport routes

Adapted from LightingLuminol (GPL-3.0, Bacteriawa, revision 72d51c4d, minecraft patch 0001 Entity#teleportAsync and portal waiter hunks marked "// LightingLuminol Start"). The region-threading base fires only its own EntityTeleportAsyncEvent / EntityPortalAsyncEvent on these routes, so pre-Folia plugins never hear a /tp, a plugin teleportAsync, the owned ASYNC route of Entity#teleport or a nether/end portal. Entity#teleportAsync now fires PlayerTeleportEvent for players on the owning thread (cancel aborts and clears the transfer state, getTo() moves the destination and is re-validated, never twice for one call: OwnedTeleport suppresses it when Paper's synchronous body already ran the event); the portal waiter fires PlayerPortalEvent once the exit is known (a moved getTo() replaces the exit; cancel places the player back in the origin world where it stood, since it is already detached). Decisions in entity/teleport/AsyncTeleportEvents; all modes; escape hatch -Daurora.compat.async-teleport-events=false.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index 603f868b5f1b0e3bc4422846966d1a5030fad45a..e94a73eb1951d0e10d636a15a21fbdf2d03a208b 100644
